               <msContents>
                  <summary>Psalter</summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1"><locus from="3r" to="141v" facs="003"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2701Dawit">Psalter</title>
                    <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                    <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.1"><locus from="3r" to="111r" facs="003"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur">Psalms of David</title>
                    <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                    <note>Each section of <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur#Ps118">Psalms of David: Psalmus 118</ref> begins with a transliterated Hebrew letter, but no statement of the <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur#Ps118Spiritual">Psalms of David: Psalm 118 including the Spritual
        Meaning of the Hebrew Letters</ref></note>
                  <note><ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur#Ps151">Psalms of David: Psalmus 151</ref> contains three of the four plusses that make up the longer edition, i.e. lacking only <foreign xml:lang="gez">ለጎልያድ፡</foreign></note>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.2"><locus from="111r" to="120v" facs="111"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1828Mahale">Book of Odes</title>
                  <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                  <note>The superscription to the fourth biblical canticle,<ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2257salota#Hannah">The Prayer of Hannah, mother of Samuel the Prophet:  Hannah</ref>, is <q> “Prayer of Hana, mother of Samuel, prophet.”</q></note>
                </msItem>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.3"><locus from="120v" to="126v" facs="121"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2362Songof">Song of Songs</title>
                  <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                  <note>Common edition</note>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.4"><locus from="127r" to="137r" facs="127"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2509Weddas">Wǝddāse Māryām</title>
                  <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                  <note>Arranged for the days of the week, beginning on Monday and culminating on Sunday</note>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.5"><locus from="137r" to="141v" facs="137"/><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1113Anqasa">ʾAnqaṣa bǝrhān</title>
                  <textLang mainLang="gez">Gǝ'ǝz</textLang>
                </msItem>
              </msItem>
               </msContents>
