                       <layout columns="1" writtenLines="22 23">
                         <locus from="2r" to="126v" facs="002"/>
                       </layout><layout subtype="computed" type="catalogue" columns="1"><writtenLines quantity="23"/></layout>
                       <layout columns="2" writtenLines="22 23">
                         <locus from="127r" to="144v" facs="127"/>
                       </layout><layout subtype="computed" type="catalogue" columns="2"><writtenLines quantity="23"/></layout>
                     </layoutDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
                  <handDesc>
                  <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                  <seg type="rubrication">
                  <foreign xml:lang="gez">ኢግዚአብሔር፡</foreign>
                  </seg>
                  <desc>The word for God is systematically rubricated</desc>
                  <desc><ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur#Ps150">Psalms of David: Psalmus 150</ref> and <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1566hababa#ThreeYouths3">Third Song of the Three Youths in the Furnace:  ThreeYouths3</ref> employ columetric rubrication</desc>
                  </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <additions>
                  <list>
                    <item xml:id="a1">
                    <locus target="#2r" facs="002"> f. 2r, top</locus>
                    <desc type="GuestText">
                    Excerpt from the book of <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2000Mazmur">Psalms of David</title>, written in black ink
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a2">
                    <locus target="#2r" facs="002"> f. 2r, bottom two lines</locus>
                    <desc>
                    pen trial or student exercise of one of the opening poems of the <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2701Dawit">Psalter</title>
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a3">
                    <locus target="#144r" facs="144"> f. 144r, column 1 and 2 top</locus>
                    <desc>
                    unidentified text, in two shades of red ink, but in the same hand
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a4">
                    <locus target="#144r" facs="144">f. 144r, column 2 bottom and 145 left</locus>
                    <desc>
                    unidentified text in black ink
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="e1">
                    <desc>
                    Several characteristics of the book suggest a private, but fairly high social location: Fine leather binding, with headband and tailband, carefully trimmed and stitched, with high quality fabric visible between the turndowns, glue residue formerly holding a mirror (?) in the back cover, Moroccan leather.  The copyist’s hand, however, is not particularly accomplished
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="e2">
                    <desc>
                    The Psalter has undergone a systematic review of initial waw’s
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="e3">
                    <desc>
                    There are several places throughout the Psalter where scribal intervention has taken place with the marginal symbol and the insertion in the upper margin
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="e4">
                    <locus target="#56r" facs="056"/>
                    <desc>
                    The midpoint of the Psalms is unmarked
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a5">
                    <locus target="#145v" facs="146"/>
                    <desc type="OwnershipNote">
                    a note of secondary ownership, with the name effaced
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                  </list>
                </additions>
                <bindingDesc>
                  <binding xml:id="binding" contemporary="true">
